# WikiRace Coding Conventions

## TypeScript
- Use `import type` for type-only imports (required by `verbatimModuleSyntax`)
- Keep types in `src/types.ts` unless tightly scoped to one file
- Prefer `useRef` for mutable game state that shouldn't trigger re-renders (clicks, path, timer start)
- Pair refs with display state: `clicksRef` (mutable) + `setClicksDisplay` (visual)

## React patterns
- Functional components only, no class components
- CSS Modules per component: `ComponentName.module.css` alongside `ComponentName.tsx`
- Custom hooks in `src/hooks/` — one concern per hook
- No router — screen switching via `type Screen = 'home' | 'game' | 'result'` in App.tsx
- Stable callbacks: use refs inside `useEffect`/`useCallback` to avoid stale closures without adding to deps

## State management
- No Redux or Zustand — local state + refs + prop drilling is sufficient
- Game session state lives in `GameScreen.tsx` (not App)
- Persistence: `localStorage` keyed by UTC date string (`"2026-03-13"`)
- Storage key: `wikirace_v1`

## Supabase
- Client is a singleton in `src/lib/supabase.ts`
- Always check `import.meta.env.VITE_SUPABASE_URL` before making requests — fall back gracefully if not configured
- Supabase writes (result submission) are fire-and-forget — never block the UI waiting for them
- Check for placeholder value: `!url.includes('your_supabase')` before attempting requests

## CSS
- Global CSS variables in `src/index.css` — never hardcode colors or fonts in component CSS
- Wikipedia article styles in `src/styles/article.css` — scoped to `.wiki-content`
- Component styles in `ComponentName.module.css` — use CSS Modules, not inline styles
- Animations defined in `index.css` as global keyframes, referenced from module CSS

## Wikipedia API
- Endpoint: `https://en.wikipedia.org/w/api.php`
- Always include `origin=*` and `redirects=1` params
- Use `parse.title` (not `displaytitle`) for canonical title comparison and win detection
- Normalize titles: `decodeURIComponent(href).replace(/_/g, ' ')` before comparing
- Link interception uses delegated events on the container — not per-link listeners

## File structure
```
src/
├── App.tsx
├── types.ts
├── main.tsx
├── index.css
├── lib/supabase.ts
├── data/fallbackPuzzles.ts
├── hooks/use*.ts
├── components/*.tsx + *.module.css
└── styles/article.css
```
